            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Jesus Christ as the ultimate, unblemished sacrifice for human sin, fulfilling the Old Testament sacrificial system (especially the Passover lamb), and reigning as the victorious, slain-yet-living King in Revelation.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"John 1:29\",\"Revelation 5:6-14\",\"Isaiah 53:7\",\"1 Corinthians 5:7\",\"1 Peter 1:19\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A fierce, apocalyptic conqueror and judge who executes God's wrath upon the wicked.\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 6:16-17\",\"Revelation 17:14\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The historical Passover sacrifice representing God's deliverance of Israel from Egypt and judgment.\",\"basis\":[\"Exodus 12:1-13\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Vulnerable followers of Christ or believers in need of pastoral care.\",\"basis\":[\"John 21:15\",\"Luke 10:3\",\"Isaiah 40:11\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The identification of 'The Lamb' (Agnus Dei) with Jesus Christ is one of the most universal and settled symbols in Christian theology, bridging the Old Testament sacrificial system with New Testament atonement theology and apocalyptic victory.\"}",
